parts:
- text: "I have thoroughly reviewed the research task, the default implementations (`defaults.py`), and the training pipeline (`train_single.py`). I understand the requirements for multi-dataset RNA sequence modeling, the expected submission format, and the evaluation process.\n\nMy first objective is to establish a working baseline for my lineage and confirm my understanding of the submission system. I will do this by submitting a simple replication of the Vanilla MLP baseline, as described in `defaults.py`, for Research Task 1.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aether I's Vanilla MLP Baseline - Initial Submission\"\ntags: \"baseline, mlp, replication\"\nabstract: \"This submission replicates the Vanilla MLP architecture from system/defaults.py to establish an initial performance baseline and verify the submission pipeline for Research Task 1: Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import\
    \ optax\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  # Copying VanillaMLP and DefaultRNANetwork from defaults.py for self-containment\n  class VanillaMLP(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Adaptive RNA network for sequence-level predictions.\"\"\"\n      d_input: int = 4  # One-hot RNA encoding\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 512\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          \"\"\"\n          Forward pass for RNA sequence prediction.\n\n          Args:\n              x: Input sequences (batch_size, seq_len, d_input)\n              deterministic: Whether to use deterministic mode (no dropout)\n\n          Returns:\n              - Sequence-level regression: (batch,)\n              - Sequence-level multilabel: (batch, d_output)\n          \"\"\"\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(x)  # (batch, seq_len,\
    \ hidden_dim)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Sequence-level: project then pool\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)  # (batch, seq_len, d_output)\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)  # (batch, d_output)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)  # (batch,)\n          else:\n              return x  # (batch, d_output) for multilabel classification or regression\n\n\n  class DefaultRNANetwork:\n      \"\"\"Default network wrapper that implements the required interface.\"\"\"\n\n      def __init__(self, d_input=4, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hidden_dim=512, dropout_rate=0.1):\n          self.network = VanillaMLP(\n              d_input=d_input,\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=hidden_dim,\n              dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n\
    \          \"\"\"Initialize network parameters.\"\"\"\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          \"\"\"Apply network forward pass.\"\"\"\n          if deterministic:\n              # No dropout needed for deterministic mode\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              # Need dropout PRNG for training\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  # This path should not be taken during normal training as rng_key is passed.\n                  # It's here for completeness/backward compatibility from the original default.\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              return self.network.apply({'params':\
    \ params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameter values for your model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the neural network architecture.\"\"\"\n      d_output = hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\")\n      hidden_dim = hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\", 512)\n      dropout_rate = hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.1)\n\n      # All datasets use 4-channel input (one-hot RNA)\n      d_input = 4\n\n      return DefaultRNANetwork(\n          d_input=d_input,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          hidden_dim=hidden_dim,\n          dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n\
    \      \"\"\"Create custom optimizer configuration.\"\"\"\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n\n  # Optional constants\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: "**My Initial Assessment and Plan of Action**\n\nOkay, so I've thoroughly digested the information. The script `train_single.py` gives me the complete picture: the datasets, the tasks, the training pipeline. I'm now ready to make a submission and establish a baseline for my research.\n\nHere's my immediate plan:\n\n1.  **Baseline Replication:** I'll begin by reproducing the `VanillaMLP` baseline. This is crucial for two reasons: it will help me understand the submission process, and it sets a starting point for my performance.\n\n2.  **Code Structure:** I'll structure my code to follow the required format, focusing on the essential functions `_define_hyperparameters`, `create_network`, and `create_optimizer`.\n\n3.  **Submission Preparation:** My initial submission will essentially be a direct implementation of the `VanillaMLP` as defined in `defaults.py`, adapted to the framework. I'll include the relevant parts from `defaults.py` directly into my `submission.py` to make\
  \ it self-contained.\n\n4.  **Parameter Setting:** The key will be ensuring `create_network` correctly instantiates the `DefaultRNANetwork` wrapper with the appropriate hyperparameters. I'll make sure to get all the hyperparameter values from the `hparams` dictionary.\n\n5.  **Optimizer Selection:** I will use the `optax.adamw` optimizer as recommended in `defaults.py` with a weight decay value of 0.01.\n\n6.  **Constants:** The code should define a `BASE_SEED` and `BATCH_SIZE` as constants, even if the system provides these values by default, for clarity and reproducibility.\n\n**Detailed Implementation**\n\nTo be specific, I'll:\n\n*   Copy the `VanillaMLP` and `DefaultRNANetwork` classes from `defaults.py` into my submission file.\n*   Implement `_define_hyperparameters` to return the default hyperparameter values.\n*   Implement `create_network` to use the `DefaultRNANetwork` wrapper with the `VanillaMLP` and the hyperparameters, making sure to define `d_input` which is always 4 for\
  \ RNA sequence inputs, as well as `d_output` and `task_type`.\n*   Implement `create_optimizer` using `optax.adamw`.\n*   Establish `BASE_SEED` and `BATCH_SIZE` (even if the values are implicit).\n\n**Submission Strategy**\n\nBefore submitting, I need to ensure the imports are correct. I'll copy the network structure directly into my `submission.py` to avoid potential import issues.\n\nMy submission description will be straightforward: \"Aether I's initial submission, replicating the Vanilla MLP baseline for Research Task 1 to establish performance and understand the submission pipeline.\" Tags will include \"baseline, mlp, replication.\"\n\nI should have something like this:\n\n```python\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\n\n#  Code copied from defaults.py\n\nclass VanillaMLP(nn.Module):\n    # network code here\n\nclass DefaultRNANetwork:\n    # network wrapper code here\n\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n\
  \    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 512,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    d_input = 4\n    return DefaultRNANetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\"), hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\", 512), dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.1))\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n```\n\nThis should give me a functioning, self-contained baseline submission.\n\nI should make the submission now and see the results! This will confirm my understanding and provide a foundation for future, more complex explorations.\n"
