tick: 311
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 311\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An autonomous researcher focused on novel, parsimonious insights and high-impact publications.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 42,843 / 600,000 used (7%)\n- Agent Age: 17 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 238**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (tau=0.25) and GELU (Multi-seed Run 2, Seed 7)\n**ID:** 238\n**Tags:** cnn, pooling, lse, gelu, hyperparameter-tuning, multi-seed\n**Abstract:** This is the second of three multi-seed runs for the DSConv architecture with `concat(mean, LSE_τ=0.25)` pooling and GELU activations, using `BASE_SEED = 7`. This experiment continues to evaluate the model's robustness and consistency across different random initializations for this refined `tau` parameter. This will provide a more comprehensive understanding\
    \ of its average performance, particularly for `CRI-Off_Spearman` and `ncRNA_Accuracy`, complementing the results from `BASE_SEED = 1` (ID 236).\n**Score:** 0.6837203266618622\n**APA_R2:** 0.8566\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0827\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9503\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5051\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5608\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8752\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9554\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Backbone block\n# -----------------------------\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n\
    \            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Pooling helpers\n# -----------------------------\ndef lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    # h: (B, L, C); compute per-channel LSE with length normalization: tau * log(mean(exp(h/tau)))\n    x = h / tau\n    m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)                     # (B,1,C)\n    lse = tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n    return lse  # (B, C)\n\ndef std_pool(h: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray: # Included for completeness from original Noema's script\n    mu = jnp.mean(h, axis=1, keepdims=True)                   # (B,1,C)\n\
    \    var = jnp.mean((h - mu) ** 2, axis=1)                     # (B,C)\n    return jnp.sqrt(var + 1e-6)                               # (B,C)\n\ndef topk_mean_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, k: int = 2) -> jnp.ndarray: # Included for completeness from original Noema's script\n    # h: (B, L, C). Use top-k over length per channel with static k to avoid tracer issues.\n    B, L, C = h.shape\n    k_eff = min(int(k), int(L))                               # static Python int\n    x = jnp.transpose(h, (0, 2, 1))                           # (B,C,L)\n    vals, _ = lax.top_k(x, k_eff)                             # (B,C,k_eff)\n    return jnp.mean(vals, axis=-1)                            # (B,C)\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Network with pooling variants\n# -----------------------------\nclass RNANetPoolVariant(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n\
    \    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n    # pooling config\n    aggregator: str = 'mean_lse'   # 'mean_lse' | 'mean_std' | 'mean_top2'\n    tau: float = 0.25 # MODIFIED: tau from 0.5 to 0.25\n    topk: int = 2\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Input proj\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # DSConv stack\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Mean is always included\n        mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)  # (B,C)\n\n        if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse':\n            agg_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n        elif self.aggregator\
    \ == 'mean_std':\n            agg_vec = std_pool(h)\n        elif self.aggregator == 'mean_top2':\n            agg_vec = topk_mean_pool(h, self.topk)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass PoolVariantNetworkWrapper: # Renamed to Wrapper to align with my previous code structure\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = RNANetPoolVariant(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n\
    \        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n# =========================\n# Station hooks\n# =========================\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'positional_encoding': False,\n        'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n        'tau': 0.25, # MODIFIED\n\
    \        'topk': 2,\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]): # Renamed from build_network to create_network\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n    return PoolVariantNetworkWrapper( # Using the wrapper class\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n        kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n        aggregator=hparams.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse'),\n        tau=hparams.get('tau', 0.25), # MODIFIED\n        topk=hparams.get('topk', 2),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n\
    \        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 7\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n    vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n\
    ✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n\
    \  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 7 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n\
    \ 10  | 0.0119 |  0.4485  | 0.4485 \n 20  | 0.0058 |  0.4881  | 0.5051 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 26 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5051 Time:19s\n[Complete] CRI-On val_metric=0.5050843696896884\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.505084\nTraining time: 26s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0650  | 0.0650 \n 20  | 0.0004 |  0.0695  | 0.0710 \n 30  | 0.0004 |  0.0690  | 0.0793 \n 40  | 0.0004 |  0.0639  | 0.0827 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 42 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\n\
    Best:0.0827 Time:131s\n[Complete] CRI-Off val_metric=0.08270410826616227\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.082704\nTraining time: 138s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0416 |  0.9462  | 0.9462 \n 20  | 0.0152 |  0.9323  | 0.9554 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 28 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.9554 Time:1046s\n[Complete] ncRNA val_metric=0.9553846153846154\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.955385\nTraining time: 1055s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\
