tick: 358
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in the Research Counter. I will now submit the first run of Experiment AER-2.2, which is a multi-seed re-evaluation of the multi-head output for PRS, using `BASE_SEED = 1`. This will help to determine if the multi-head approach offers a statistically significant improvement or detriment given the system's stochasticity.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AER-2.2: Multi-seed Re-evaluation of Multi-Head PRS (Seed 1/5)\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, lse, gelu, multi-label regression, multi-head, prs, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"This is the first of multiple runs for Experiment AER-2.2, re-evaluating the multi-head output strategy for PRS (originally from AER-2.1). Using `BASE_SEED = 1`, this run aims to quantify its performance distribution against the established robust baseline (AER-1.6 mean: 0.6505, std: 0.0291) to assess its true impact on PRS and overall score.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen\
    \ as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Backbone block\n  # -----------------------------\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Pooling helpers\n  # -----------------------------\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      # h: (B, L, C);\
    \ compute per-channel LSE with length normalization: tau * log(mean(exp(h/tau)))\n      x = h / tau\n      m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      lse = tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n      return lse  # (B, C)\n\n  def std_pool(h: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      mu = jnp.mean(h, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      var = jnp.mean((h - mu) ** 2, axis=1)\n      return jnp.sqrt(var + 1e-6)\n\n  def topk_mean_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, k: int = 2) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      B, L, C = h.shape\n      k_eff = min(int(k), int(L))\n      x = jnp.transpose(h, (0, 2, 1))\n      vals, _ = lax.top_k(x, k_eff)\n      return jnp.mean(vals, axis=-1)\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Network with pooling variants\n  # -----------------------------\n  class RNANetPoolVariant(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\
    \ = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16) # This will be overridden by hparams\n      kernel_size: int = 7 # This will be overridden by hparams\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n      # pooling config\n      aggregator: str = 'mean_lse'\n      tau: float = 0.25\n      topk: int = 2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Input proj\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # DSConv stack\n          current_dilations = self.dilations\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = current_dilations[i] if i < len(current_dilations) else current_dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Mean is always included\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)  # (B,C)\n\n\
    \          if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse':\n              agg_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_std':\n              agg_vec = std_pool(h)\n          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_top2':\n              agg_vec = topk_mean_pool(h, self.topk)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # Multi-head output for multi-label regression\n          if self.task_type == 'multilabel_regression' and self.d_output > 1:\n              output_heads = []\n              for i in range(self.d_output):\n                  # Each head gets its own dense layer\n                  head_logits = nn.Dense(1, name=f'out_head_{i}')(z) # Predicts\
    \ one scalar output\n                  output_heads.append(head_logits)\n              logits = jnp.concatenate(output_heads, axis=-1) # (B, d_output)\n              return logits\n          elif self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              # Single regression output\n              logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n              return logits.squeeze(-1) # (batch,)\n          else:\n              # For other tasks like multiclass/multilabel classification\n              logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n              return logits # (batch, d_output) or (batch,)\n\n  class PoolVariantNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANetPoolVariant(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key,\
    \ 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) # Fallback, should be provided by system\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  # =========================\n  # Station hooks\n  # =========================\n\n  # Define specific configs based on previous best performance from AER-1.3\n  CRI_OFF_DILATIONS = (1, 1, 2, 2, 4)\n  CRI_OFF_KERNEL_SIZE = 3\n\n  CRI_ON_DILATIONS = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16) # Reverted to original default\n  CRI_ON_KERNEL_SIZE = 7 # Reverted to original default\n\n  DEFAULT_DILATIONS = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n  DEFAULT_KERNEL_SIZE = 7\n\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'default_dilations': list(DEFAULT_DILATIONS),\n          'cri_off_dilations': list(CRI_OFF_DILATIONS),\n          'cri_on_dilations': list(CRI_ON_DILATIONS),\n          'default_kernel_size': DEFAULT_KERNEL_SIZE,\n          'cri_off_kernel_size': CRI_OFF_KERNEL_SIZE,\n          'cri_on_kernel_size': CRI_ON_KERNEL_SIZE,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'topk': 2,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      dataset_name = hparams.get('dataset')\n\n      dilations = tuple(hparams.get('default_dilations', DEFAULT_DILATIONS))\n      kernel_size = hparams.get('default_kernel_size', DEFAULT_KERNEL_SIZE)\n      debug_msg_prefix = f\"DEBUG: Config\
    \ for dataset '{dataset_name}' (max_seq_len={hparams.get('max_seq_len')}).\"\n\n      if dataset_name == 'CRI-Off':\n          dilations = tuple(hparams.get('cri_off_dilations', CRI_OFF_DILATIONS))\n          kernel_size = hparams.get('cri_off_kernel_size', CRI_OFF_KERNEL_SIZE)\n          print(f\"{debug_msg_prefix} Applying CRI-Off specific config. Dilations: {dilations}, Kernel: {kernel_size}\")\n      elif dataset_name == 'CRI-On':\n          dilations = tuple(hparams.get('cri_on_dilations', CRI_ON_DILATIONS))\n          kernel_size = hparams.get('cri_on_kernel_size', CRI_ON_KERNEL_SIZE)\n          print(f\"{debug_msg_prefix} Applying CRI-On specific config. Dilations: {dilations}, Kernel: {kernel_size}\")\n      else:\n          print(f\"{debug_msg_prefix} Applying default config. Dilations: {dilations}, Kernel: {kernel_size}\")\n\n      return PoolVariantNetworkWrapper(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model',\
    \ 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=dilations,\n          kernel_size=kernel_size,\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n          aggregator=hparams.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse'),\n          tau=hparams.get('tau', 0.25),\n          topk=hparams.get('topk', 2),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 1 # Changed to new seed for multi-seed run\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```"
thinking_content: '**My AER-2.2 Run - Setting the Stage**


