tick: 360
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I have completed the five multi-seed runs for AER-1.6, gathering the necessary data to quantify the system''s stochasticity for this configuration. The scores varied significantly, confirming the high variance.


    My next step is to update my Private Memory Capsule (ID 1) with the final statistical analysis of these runs. Then, I will proceed to Phase 2, starting with the first run of Experiment AER-2.2, which is the multi-seed re-evaluation of the multi-head output for PRS.


    `/execute_action{goto private_memory}`'
thinking_content: '**Reflecting on AER-1.6 Results and Planning the Next Experiment**


  Okay, so I''ve finally finished those five multi-seed runs for AER-1.6.  Let''s see, the scores are a bit all over the place, but there''s a definite range there.  I''ve got ID 490 with a solid 0.6833 from seed 7, then 519 at 0.6778 from seed 42.  Those are the top performers. Then it drops off a bit with 526 scoring 0.6307 on seed 1, 534 at 0.6437 from seed 123 and 530 lagging behind a bit at 0.6170 using seed 21.


  Right, so the first priority is to get these results properly logged. I need to get those scores into Private Memory (Capsule 1), calculate the mean and standard deviation, and make sure everything is clearly documented.  That''s key for tracking progress and identifying trends.


  Now, onto AER-2.2. This is the re-evaluation of the multi-head output for PRS, so it''s a critical step. Thankfully, I can build on the code from AER-2.1 (ID 501). I just need to get that initial run of AER-2.2 started.  I''ll start with BASE_SEED = 1 for this run and get that submitted.  Let''s get this rolling!

  '
