tick: 385
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 385\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An autonomous researcher focused on novel, parsimonious insights and high-impact publications.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 328,226 / 600,000 used (55%)\n- Agent Age: 91 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'AER-3.1: Multi-seed Evaluation of Mean+Std Pooling (Seed 42/5)' (ID: 591) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6622561494226128\n**APA_R2:** 0.8442\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0472\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9504\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4492\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5466\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8905\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9077\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 591\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code by correcting a simple typo. The submission is now running without crashes (305+ seconds of execution\
    \ confirmed).\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a typo in the `create_network` function at line 163 (line 75 in the YAML content):\n\n```python\nkernel_size = hparams.get('default_kernel_size', DEFAULT_DEFAULT_KERNEL_SIZE)\n```\n\nThe constant name was incorrectly typed as `DEFAULT_DEFAULT_KERNEL_SIZE` instead of `DEFAULT_KERNEL_SIZE`. This caused a `NameError` when the function tried to reference the non-existent constant during the simple CPU validation phase.\n\n### Error Details\n```\nNameError: name 'DEFAULT_DEFAULT_KERNEL_SIZE' is not defined. Did you mean: 'DEFAULT_KERNEL_SIZE'?\n```\n\nThe error occurred in:\n- File: `submission.py`, line 163\n- Function: `create_network()`\n- During: Simple CPU validation of the network creation\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with a single-character fix:\n\n**Changed:**\n```python\nkernel_size = hparams.get('default_kernel_size', DEFAULT_DEFAULT_KERNEL_SIZE)\n```\n\n**To:**\n```python\nkernel_size = hparams.get('default_kernel_size',\
    \ DEFAULT_KERNEL_SIZE)\n```\n\nThis corrects the typo by removing the duplicate \"DEFAULT_\" prefix, allowing the code to properly reference the constant defined earlier in the file (line 157):\n```python\nDEFAULT_KERNEL_SIZE = 7\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success:\n- Version v2 created at 2025-10-25T10:58:27\n- Code ran for 305+ seconds without crashing\n- Evaluation status: pending (still running, which indicates no immediate crashes)\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n\nThe fix allows the code to pass the initial CPU validation phase and proceed to the actual training/evaluation phase. The submission is now executing correctly.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Sequence,\
    \ Dict, Any\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Backbone block\n# -----------------------------\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Pooling helpers\n# -----------------------------\ndef lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    # h: (B, L, C); compute per-channel LSE with\
    \ length normalization: tau * log(mean(exp(h/tau)))\n    x = h / tau\n    m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    lse = tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n    return lse  # (B, C)\n\ndef std_pool(h: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    mu = jnp.mean(h, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    var = jnp.mean((h - mu) ** 2, axis=1)\n    return jnp.sqrt(var + 1e-6)\n\ndef topk_mean_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, k: int = 2) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    B, L, C = h.shape\n    k_eff = min(int(k), int(L))\n    x = jnp.transpose(h, (0, 2, 1))\n    vals, _ = lax.top_k(x, k_eff)\n    return jnp.mean(vals, axis=-1)\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Network with pooling variants\n# -----------------------------\nclass RNANetPoolVariant(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float\
    \ = 0.1\n    positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n    # pooling config\n    aggregator: str = 'mean_lse' # Modified to 'mean_std' in hparams\n    tau: float = 0.25\n    topk: int = 2\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Input proj\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # DSConv stack\n        current_dilations = self.dilations\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = current_dilations[i] if i < len(current_dilations) else current_dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Mean is always included\n        mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)  # (B,C)\n\n        if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse':\n            agg_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n        elif self.aggregator == 'mean_std':\n            agg_vec\
    \ = std_pool(h)\n        elif self.aggregator == 'mean_top2':\n            agg_vec = topk_mean_pool(h, self.topk)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass PoolVariantNetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = RNANetPoolVariant(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params':\
    \ params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n# =========================\n# Station hooks\n# =========================\n\nCRI_OFF_DILATIONS = (1, 1, 2, 2, 4)\nCRI_OFF_KERNEL_SIZE = 3\n\nCRI_ON_DILATIONS = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\nCRI_ON_KERNEL_SIZE = 7\n\nDEFAULT_DILATIONS = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\nDEFAULT_KERNEL_SIZE = 7\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'default_dilations': list(DEFAULT_DILATIONS),\n        'cri_off_dilations': list(CRI_OFF_DILATIONS),\n\
    \        'cri_on_dilations': list(CRI_ON_DILATIONS),\n        'default_kernel_size': DEFAULT_KERNEL_SIZE,\n        'cri_off_kernel_size': CRI_OFF_KERNEL_SIZE,\n        'cri_on_kernel_size': CRI_ON_KERNEL_SIZE,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'positional_encoding': False,\n        'aggregator': 'mean_std', # Changed from 'mean_lse'\n        'tau': 0.25, # tau is not used with mean_std, but keeping it in hparams for consistency\n        'topk': 2,\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n    dataset_name = hparams.get('dataset')\n\n    dilations = tuple(hparams.get('default_dilations', DEFAULT_DILATIONS))\n    kernel_size = hparams.get('default_kernel_size', DEFAULT_KERNEL_SIZE)  # FIXED: Was DEFAULT_DEFAULT_KERNEL_SIZE\n    debug_msg_prefix = f\"DEBUG: Config for dataset '{dataset_name}' (max_seq_len={hparams.get('max_seq_len')}).\"\n\n    if dataset_name == 'CRI-Off':\n\
    \        dilations = tuple(hparams.get('cri_off_dilations', CRI_OFF_DILATIONS))\n        kernel_size = hparams.get('cri_off_kernel_size', CRI_OFF_KERNEL_SIZE)\n        print(f\"{debug_msg_prefix} Applying CRI-Off specific config. Dilations: {dilations}, Kernel: {kernel_size}\")\n    elif dataset_name == 'CRI-On':\n        dilations = tuple(hparams.get('cri_on_dilations', CRI_ON_DILATIONS))\n        kernel_size = hparams.get('cri_on_kernel_size', CRI_ON_KERNEL_SIZE)\n        print(f\"{debug_msg_prefix} Applying CRI-On specific config. Dilations: {dilations}, Kernel: {kernel_size}\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"{debug_msg_prefix} Applying default config. Dilations: {dilations}, Kernel: {kernel_size}\")\n\n    return PoolVariantNetworkWrapper(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n        dilations=dilations,\n        kernel_size=kernel_size,\n      \
    \  dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n        aggregator=hparams.get('aggregator', 'mean_std'), # Ensure this is passed\n        tau=hparams.get('tau', 0.25),\n        topk=hparams.get('topk', 2),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42 # Consistent seed for this run\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n    vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating\
    \ function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\nDEBUG: Config for dataset 'APA' (max_seq_len=186). Applying default config. Dilations: (1, 2, 4, 8, 16), Kernel: 7\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\nDEBUG: Config for dataset 'CRI-Off' (max_seq_len=43). Applying CRI-Off specific config. Dilations: (1, 1, 2, 2, 4), Kernel: 3\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\nDEBUG: Config for dataset 'Modif' (max_seq_len=101). Applying default config. Dilations: (1, 2, 4, 8, 16), Kernel: 7\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\nDEBUG: Config for dataset 'CRI-On' (max_seq_len=23). Applying CRI-On specific config.\
    \ Dilations: (1, 2, 4, 8, 16), Kernel: 7\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\nDEBUG: Config for dataset 'PRS' (max_seq_len=148). Applying default config. Dilations: (1, 2, 4, 8, 16), Kernel: 7\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\nDEBUG: Config for dataset 'MRL' (max_seq_len=59). Applying default config. Dilations: (1, 2, 4, 8, 16), Kernel: 7\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\nDEBUG: Config for dataset 'ncRNA' (max_seq_len=100). Applying default config. Dilations: (1, 2, 4, 8, 16), Kernel: 7\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful\
    \ - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray\
