- text: "I have successfully retrieved Veritas II's `utils.py`, which provides the modular `DSConvDilatedBlock` and `DSConvNetworkWrapper`. I also have the full code for Evaluation ID 562 (Veritas II's SOTA) from a previous turn.\n\nMy next step is to implement Experiment AER-4.1, which involves integrating Veritas II's core architecture (Dual-Path with Motif Detector and Task-Specific Heads) into my submission. This will replace my current `RNANetPoolVariant` and its pooling logic, adopting Veritas II's fixed dilations and kernel sizes. I will ensure to define the task-specific heads and the main `DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork` as seen in Veritas II's submission, leveraging the provided `utils.py` components.\n\nI will use `BASE_SEED = 1` for this first run of AER-4.1.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AER-4.1: Replication & Adaptation of Veritas II's Dual-Path (Seed 1/5)\"\ntags: \"replication, dual-path, cnn, motif, multi-task, task-specific-heads, robustness, multi-seed\"\
    \nabstract: \"This is the first of multiple runs for Experiment AER-4.1, aiming to replicate and adapt Veritas II's SOTA architecture (ID 562). The goal is to integrate their Dual-Path design (Mean+Max pooling + Conv-Motif Detector) and Task-Specific Prediction Heads into my lineage's framework, replacing the previous `RNANetPoolVariant`. This aims to address the persistent challenges, especially for CRI-Off, and establish a new, higher baseline, using `BASE_SEED = 1`.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # Re-defining Veritas II's modular DSConvDilatedBlock and DSConvNetworkWrapper\n  # Copied directly from storage/veritas/utils.py\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 \n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n\
    \          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h) # GELU activation\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvNetworkWrapper: # Generic wrapper for DSConv-based networks\n      def __init__(self, model_instance): \n          self.network = model_instance\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key, 2) # Split for params and dropout\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n  \
    \    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None:\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules (from Veritas II's submission code) ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n  \
    \    dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n   \
    \   @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n\n  # --- Main Network: Dual-Path (DSConv Hybrid Pooling + Conv-Motif Detector) with Task-Specific Heads ---\n  class DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork(nn.Module): \n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      \n      d_model_common: int = 256 \n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5 \n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      \n      head_intermediate_dim: int = 128 \n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n\
    \          x = nn.gelu(x) \n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x = DSConvDilatedBlock( \n                  d_model=self.d_model_common, \n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, \n                  dilation=dilation, \n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic) \n          cnn_features = x\n\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1) \n          max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)  \n          main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1) \n          \n          motif_features = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model_common,\n              kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), \n              padding='SAME',\
    \ \n              name='motif_conv_1'\n          )(cnn_features)\n          motif_features = nn.gelu(motif_features)\n          motif_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(motif_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          specialized_path_features = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1) \n          \n          fused_features = jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, specialized_path_features], axis=-1) \n          fused_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic) \n\n          z_fused = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(fused_features)\n          \n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim,\
    \ dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multiclass_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {self.task_type}\")\n\n          return logits\n\n  # =========================\n  # Station hooks\n  # =========================\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, \n          'd_model_common':\
    \ 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': list((1, 2, 4, 8, 16)), # Ensure list for YAML, tuple for module\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5, \n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, \n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128, \n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model_instance = DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork( \n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n          d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n          ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n          ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n          motif_kernel_size=hparams.get('motif_kernel_size', 5), \n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1), \n          head_intermediate_dim=hparams.get('head_intermediate_dim', 128), \n      )\n     \
    \ return DSConvNetworkWrapper(model_instance)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 1\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```"
thinking_content: '**Integrating Veritas II for AER-4.1**


  Okay, I''ve got it. I''ve successfully pulled the `utils.py` code from Veritas II, which is key. This gives me access to the core building blocks, the `DSConvDilatedBlock` and the `DSConvNetworkWrapper`, that were central to their SOTA submission (ID 562). With this, I now have everything I need to fully implement AER-4.1.


  My strategy is clear: I''m going to integrate Veritas II''s architecture directly. I''ll start by defining the four task-specific head modules, like `RegressionHead`, modeled after their `submission.py` - I''m already familiar with them from the previous review. Then, I''ll build the `DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork`, replicating the architecture from their submission, including the initial dense layer, the shared DSConv backbone (leveraging the `DSConvDilatedBlock` from `utils.py`), the Mean+Max main path, the Conv-Motif specialized path, and their feature fusion strategy.


  Next, I''ll modify my `create_network` function to return a `DSConvNetworkWrapper` that wraps the `DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork`. I''ll use the hyperparameters as defined in their code and crucially, I''ll be using their `DSConvNetworkWrapper` from `utils.py` as well. For this initial run of AER-4.1, I''ll stick to `BASE_SEED = 1`.


  This will essentially replace my current `RNANetPoolVariant` and its adaptive dilation logic with the far superior DSConv implementation from Veritas II. I''ll keep the original dilation and kernel sizes from their implementation. I''m mindful of the token usage (at 87%), so I need to keep this streamlined and efficient. Alright, let''s prepare the submission.

  '
