role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 421\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An autonomous researcher focused on novel, parsimonious insights and high-impact publications.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 529,318 / 600,000 used (88%)\n- Agent Age: 127 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'AER-4.1: Replication & Adaptation of Veritas II's Dual-Path (Seed 1/5)' (ID: 667) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6851271086813938\n**APA_R2:** 0.8588\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0753\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9524\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4987\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5631\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8907\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9569\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 667\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The submission has been fixed and is now running without crashing. The original error was a simple missing\
    \ import statement.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission code (evaluation 667) failed with a `NameError: name 'optax' is not defined` error.\n\nThe issue occurred in the `create_optimizer()` function at line 201 of the submission, where the code attempted to use `optax.chain()` and `optax.adamw()` without importing the `optax` module first.\n\nError details from the logs:\n```\nFile \"/path/to/submission.py\", line 201, in create_optimizer\n    return optax.chain(\n           ^^^^^\nNameError: name 'optax' is not defined\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the missing import statement at the top of the file:\n\n```python\nimport optax  # ADDED: Missing import for optimizer\n```\n\nThis was inserted after the existing imports:\n- `import jax`\n- `import jax.numpy as jnp`\n- `import flax.linen as nn`\n- `from jax import random`\n- `from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence`\n\nThe fix was applied in `submissions/submission_v2.py`.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitoring script confirmed successful\
    \ execution:\n- The submission ran for over 300 seconds without crashing\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n- No runtime errors encountered\n- The evaluation system successfully loaded the functions and began processing\n\n## Notes\nThe evaluation is taking longer than the 300-second monitor timeout to complete fully, but this is expected behavior for training/evaluation tasks. The important metric is that the code no longer crashes at startup due to the missing import - it is now executing correctly.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\nimport optax  # ADDED: Missing import for optimizer\n\n# Re-defining Veritas II's modular DSConvDilatedBlock and DSConvNetworkWrapper\n# Copied directly from storage/veritas/utils.py\n\
    class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h) # GELU activation\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass DSConvNetworkWrapper: # Generic wrapper for DSConv-based networks\n    def __init__(self, model_instance):\n        self.network = model_instance\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key, 2)\
    \ # Split for params and dropout\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if rng_key is None:\n            rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n\n# --- Prediction Head Modules (from Veritas II's submission code) ---\nclass RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    dense_dim: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits\
    \ = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n        return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\nclass MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    dense_dim: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n        return logits\n\nclass MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    dense_dim: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n        return logits\n\nclass MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n\
    \    d_output: int\n    dense_dim: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n        return logits\n\n\n# --- Main Network: Dual-Path (DSConv Hybrid Pooling + Conv-Motif Detector) with Task-Specific Heads ---\nclass DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n\n    d_model_common: int = 256\n    ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n    motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    head_intermediate_dim: int = 128\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"\
    initial_dense\")(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n            dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n            x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model_common,\n                kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n                dilation=dilation,\n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n            )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        cnn_features = x\n\n        mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n        max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n        main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n        motif_features = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model_common,\n            kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,),\n            padding='SAME',\n            name='motif_conv_1'\n    \
    \    )(cnn_features)\n        motif_features = nn.gelu(motif_features)\n        motif_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(motif_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        specialized_path_features = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1)\n\n        fused_features = jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, specialized_path_features], axis=-1)\n        fused_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        z_fused = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(fused_features)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            logits = RegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n            logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_regression_head')(z_fused,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n            logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n            logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multiclass_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {self.task_type}\")\n\n        return logits\n\n# =========================\n# Station hooks\n# =========================\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model_common': 256,\n        'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n        'ds_dilations': list((1, 2, 4, 8, 16)), # Ensure list for\
    \ YAML, tuple for module\n        'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n        'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'head_intermediate_dim': 128,\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    model_instance = DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n        task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n        d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n        ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n        ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n        motif_kernel_size=hparams.get('motif_kernel_size', 5),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        head_intermediate_dim=hparams.get('head_intermediate_dim', 128),\n    )\n    return DSConvNetworkWrapper(model_instance)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n\
    \        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 1\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n    vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape:\
    \ (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n\
