role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in the Private Memory Room and have successfully updated Capsule 1 with the latest analysis and my detailed plan for Experiment AER-4.2. My token budget is at a critical 95% usage. I need to be extremely cautious.\n\nI will proceed to the Research Counter to submit the first run of Experiment AER-4.2 (direct replication of Veritas II's ID 562, using their import path for modular components), with `BASE_SEED = 1`. This is a crucial diagnostic step.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AER-4.2: Direct Replication of Veritas II's ID 562 (Seed 1/5) - With Import\"\ntags: \"replication, dual-path, cnn, motif, multi-task, task-specific-heads, reproducibility, multi-seed\"\nabstract: \"This is the first of multiple runs for Experiment AER-4.2, aiming for a direct, precise replication of Veritas II's SOTA (ID 562). This attempt utilizes Veritas II's original modular import strategy (`sys.path.append('storage/veritas')` and `from utils\
    \ import ...`) for `DSConvDilatedBlock` and `DSConvNetworkWrapper`, addressing a potential source of discrepancy in CRI-Off performance. Using `BASE_SEED = 1`, this run will assess if this setup recovers Veritas II's high CRI-Off score (0.1365).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/veritas') # VERITAS II's original import statement\n  from utils import DSConvDilatedBlock, DSConvNetworkWrapper # Reusing modular components\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules (from Veritas II's submission code) ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output,\
    \ name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n\n  # --- Main Network: Dual-Path (DSConv Hybrid Pooling + Conv-Motif Detector) with Task-Specific Heads ---\n  class DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork(nn.Module): \n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      \n      d_model_common: int = 256 \n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5 \n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    \
    \  \n      head_intermediate_dim: int = 128 \n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x) \n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x = DSConvDilatedBlock( \n                  d_model=self.d_model_common, \n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, \n                  dilation=dilation, \n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic) \n          cnn_features = x\n\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1) \n          max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)  \n          main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\
    \ \n          \n          motif_features = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model_common,\n              kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), \n              padding='SAME', \n              name='motif_conv_1'\n          )(cnn_features)\n          motif_features = nn.gelu(motif_features)\n          motif_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(motif_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          specialized_path_features = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1) \n          \n          fused_features = jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, specialized_path_features], axis=-1) \n          fused_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic) \n\n          z_fused = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(fused_features)\n          \n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='regression_head')(z_fused,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multiclass_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {self.task_type}\")\n\n          return logits\n\
    \n  # =========================\n  # Station hooks\n  # =========================\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, \n          'd_model_common': 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': list((1, 2, 4, 8, 16)),\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5, \n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, \n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128, \n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model_instance = DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork( \n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n          d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n          ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5), \n          ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n          motif_kernel_size=hparams.get('motif_kernel_size',\
    \ 5), \n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1), \n          head_intermediate_dim=hparams.get('head_intermediate_dim', 128), \n      )\n      return DSConvNetworkWrapper(model_instance)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 1\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```"
