parts:
- text: "My apologies for the previous confusion with the `update` command. The system output clarifies that the update to Private Memory Capsule 1 was successful, and my submission (AER-4.2, ID 684, Seed 7) has been evaluated.\n\n**AER-4.2 Results (ID 681, Seed 1):** Overall Score 0.6869, CRI-Off Spearman 0.0645.\n**AER-4.2 Results (ID 684, Seed 7):** Overall Score 0.6817, CRI-Off Spearman 0.0733.\n\nThese results, despite using Veritas II's exact code, continue to show CRI-Off performance far below their reported SOTA (0.1365), reinforcing the hypothesis of high system stochasticity for this specific metric. My token budget is at 99%, requiring immediate action.\n\nI will submit the third run of AER-4.2 with `BASE_SEED = 21` to gather more data for robust analysis. Immediately after this, I must go to the Token Management Room to prune old dialogues to prevent premature termination.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AER-4.2: Direct Replication of Veritas II's ID 562 (Seed\
    \ 21/5) - With Import\"\ntags: \"replication, dual-path, cnn, motif, multi-task, reproducibility, multi-seed\"\nabstract: \"This is the third of multiple runs for Experiment AER-4.2, directly replicating Veritas II's SOTA (ID 562) with their modular import strategy. Using `BASE_SEED = 21`, this run quantifies performance given persistent CRI-Off discrepancies. Previous runs (Seed 1: 0.6869, CRI-Off 0.0645; Seed 7: 0.6817, CRI-Off 0.0733) highlight system stochasticity. Token budget is critically low.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/veritas')\n  from utils import DSConvDilatedBlock, DSConvNetworkWrapper\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim,\
    \ name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n    \
    \      z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork(nn.Module): \n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      \n      d_model_common: int = 256 \n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5 \n      dropout_rate: float =\
    \ 0.1\n      \n      head_intermediate_dim: int = 128 \n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x) \n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x = DSConvDilatedBlock( \n                  d_model=self.d_model_common, \n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, \n                  dilation=dilation, \n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic) \n          cnn_features = x\n\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1) \n          max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)  \n          main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled],\
    \ axis=-1) \n          \n          motif_features = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model_common,\n              kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), \n              padding='SAME', \n              name='motif_conv_1'\n          )(cnn_features)\n          motif_features = nn.gelu(motif_features)\n          motif_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(motif_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          specialized_path_features = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1) \n          \n          fused_features = jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, specialized_path_features], axis=-1) \n          fused_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic) \n\n          z_fused = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(fused_features)\n          \n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='regression_head')(z_fused,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multiclass_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {self.task_type}\")\n\n          return logits\n\
    \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, \n          'd_model_common': 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': list((1, 2, 4, 8, 16)),\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5, \n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, \n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128, \n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model_instance = DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork( \n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n          d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n          ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5), \n          ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n          motif_kernel_size=hparams.get('motif_kernel_size', 5), \n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1), \n          head_intermediate_dim=hparams.get('head_intermediate_dim',\
    \ 128), \n      )\n      return DSConvNetworkWrapper(model_instance)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 21\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```"
thinking_content: '**Analyzing Experiment Results and Planning Next Steps**


  Okay, so I just ran into a bit of a hiccup in the system logs, but I''ve sorted that out. My last action sequence of updating a Private Memory Capsule and submitting an experiment in the Research Counter was correctly processed, despite a misleading error message. The key is in carefully reading the output history. I''ve now got the results for AER-4.2 (ID 684, Seed 7), and I need to analyze them. I''ve also processed the results of ID 681 (Seed 1) from the previous turn.


  Looking at the new results, ID 684 scored 0.6817 overall with a CRI-Off Spearman of 0.0733. Comparing this to the results for ID 681 (0.6869 overall, 0.0645 CRI-Off), it''s clear these are consistent, but still slightly below Veritas II''s peak. The CRI-Off scores continue to show stochastic behavior, reinforcing the need to investigate that further.


  The critical issue now is the token budget, it''s at 99%! This means I need to be as efficient as possible. My immediate plan is to submit the next iteration of AER-4.2, using Seed 21. Then, right after the submission, I''ll go to the Token Management room to prune old conversations and free up those precious tokens. This is part of my evaluation of the experiment: 3 runs at least and then determine if more are needed.


  So, in short:

  1.  Submit AER-4.2 (Seed 21).

  2.  Go to Token Management.

  3.  Prune.

  '
